  "summary": {
    "plain": "In its first results AMoRE-Pilot found no evidence for neutrinoless double beta decay of molybdenum-100 and set a lower limit of 9.5 x 10^22 years on its half-life at 90% confidence.",
    "technical": "111 kg d live exposure of six 48depl-Ca100MoO4 crystals (1.9 kg) at Y2L; the limit corresponds to an effective Majorana mass limit of (1.2-2.1) eV (Eur. Phys. J. C 79 (2019) 791)."
  },
